00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:05,472
Letters name blocks, while H and V describe how two regions combine.

2
00:00:06,562 --> 00:00:10,794
Push A, then push D; D is now on top of the stack.

3
00:00:11,884 --> 00:00:16,764
H names a horizontal cut, placing the first region below the second.

4
00:00:18,504 --> 00:00:25,208
Pop D first, then A; place D above A to obtain a three-by-three region.

5
00:00:26,298 --> 00:00:33,698
Use V to add B, C, and E in order, producing a nine-by-three bounding box.

6
00:00:34,788 --> 00:00:40,268
Change the first H to V; the blocks form a row whose total width is twelve.

7
00:00:41,358 --> 00:00:48,230
One stack item only passes the structural check; it cannot replace ID checks or outline checks.

8
00:00:49,320 --> 00:00:55,640
Read the tokens one at a time in the lab, inspect the stack, and construct another legal layout.
